cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use astro-duck in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "astro-duck: A DuckDB extension for astronomical calculations"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Björn
    family-names: Bethge
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4500-0274"
repository-code: "https://github.com/synapticore-io/astro-duck"
url: "https://github.com/synapticore-io/astro-duck"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: "2026-04-09"
abstract: >-
  astro-duck is a DuckDB extension that brings astronomical
  calculations to SQL: coordinate transforms (RA/Dec to Cartesian,
  ICRS to galactic frames), angular separation on the celestial
  sphere, photometric conversions (magnitude/flux, distance modulus,
  absolute magnitude), CCM89 + O'Donnell 1994 dust extinction with
  standard UBVRIJHK photometric bands, cosmological distances
  (luminosity, comoving), celestial body models (main-sequence stars,
  white dwarfs, neutron stars, black holes, brown dwarfs, rocky
  planets, gas giants, ice giants, asteroids), Keplerian orbital
  mechanics, 3D octree spatial indexing, and Newtonian gravitational
  dynamics. It is designed for vectorized batch processing of
  astronomical catalogs (Gaia DR3, SDSS, NASA Exoplanet Archive,
  simulation snapshots) directly from Parquet files in a single
  DuckDB process.
keywords:
  - duckdb
  - duckdb-extension
  - astronomy
  - astrophysics
  - sql
  - coordinates
  - photometry
  - cosmology
  - dust-extinction
  - ccm89
  - orbital-mechanics
